  "id": "tool-design",
  "term": "tool design",
  "definition": "Tool design is the way a hand tool is shaped and put together so it matches the task, the user, and the setting where it is used. In this source, it includes technical features such as weight, handle size, and the fit of parts, along with practical and cultural factors that affect efficient use, comfort, maintenance, and user satisfaction.",
